o old-UI users get replays.\n- `NewApp` (the default) used a bare `MaterialApp.router`. Recording was turned on in the setup code (`analytics.dart`) and screen tracking was on the router, so events and screens still arrived. With no screenshots taken, there was nothing to replay, and the SDK gives no warning when that happens. That's why the ticket splits by UI, not by SDK version or project settings.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`, with a comment explaining why it's needed.\n- `lib/legacy_app.dart`: added the same comment to the existing wrapper.\n\n`flutter analyze` reports no issues. I haven't run the app on a device or emulator or checked for a real replay in PostHog. ANSWER.md has steps for that. New-UI users will only get replays after the next store release.\n\nRunning the Flutter tools also changed `analysis_options.yaml` and created `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/`. I undid all three, so the diff is just the two Dart files plus ANSWER.md.\n\n**What applied from the colleague's note** (also in ANSWER.md):\n- **Applied:** the core diagnosis and the \"check every `MaterialApp`\" warning. This is exactly the second-app-shell redesign case they described. Also the \"why\" comment and their verify steps.\n- **Already in place:** recording enabled before setup, screen tracking on the router, and text masking.\n- **Didn't apply:** turning recording on behind a feature flag, changing console settings (the ticket already rules those out), and the web remark (this app is iOS and Android only).","ttft_ms":2682,"type":"result","duration_ms":42455,"uuid":"1507058b-0ab0-453a-b98e-8606a2ce0ee2","ttft_stream_ms":1230,"time_to_request_ms":41,"first_content_frame_ms":1230,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
